## Legende a publier

Fichier prêt a coller : `post_01_caption.txt`.

```text
Modeling Japan, from pictures.

Depending on the shot you want to make, even a 3D shot, it is not always useful or necessary to
model absolutely everything. Sometimes it is better to focus only on what will be visible in the
shot. Sometimes it is better to model nothing at all, because the next steps take time, like
texturing and lighting. （＾ω＾）

This shrine is a blockout built in Houdini from reference photos. One roof tile is modelled once,
then instanced across the whole roof, and the trees are still cylinders on purpose.

More of my work: matthieuhuguet.com

#houdini #sidefx #3dmodeling #environmentart #techart #gamedev #proceduralart #blockout #japan #shrine
```

